272
00:12:44,052 --> 00:12:47,052
Because everybody in the world loves me, too!

273
00:12:47,052 --> 00:12:50,052
That includes me, dearest Lady Lily.

274
00:12:51,052 --> 00:12:52,052
Saki will be okay.

275
00:12:52,052 --> 00:12:53,052
Just give her space.

276
00:12:57,052 --> 00:13:00,052
This one comes from Saga PD's Dirty Harry.

277
00:13:01,052 --> 00:13:02,052
Back for more, huh?

278
00:13:03,052 --> 00:13:04,052
Good evening, Ryu.

279
00:13:04,052 --> 00:13:07,052
My favorite bar just hired this cute new bartender.

280
00:13:07,052 --> 00:13:10,052
A classy lady who's got an old-fashioned way about her.

281
00:13:10,052 --> 00:13:12,052
She's giving me strong signals.

282
00:13:12,052 --> 00:13:14,052
I think maybe she's kind of into me.

283
00:13:15,052 --> 00:13:16,052
Enough of that crap.

284
00:13:16,052 --> 00:13:17,052
Time for a song.

285
00:13:17,052 --> 00:13:20,052
White Ryu with Do You Hate Windy Days.

286
00:13:21,052 --> 00:13:22,052
Hey, Saki.

287
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,052
Sorry that I got you guys all freaked out.

288
00:13:27,052 --> 00:13:30,052
The first time I heard about Ryu, I was a middle schooler.

289
00:13:32,052 --> 00:13:35,052
Back then, I used to feel like the whole damn world was out to get me.

290
00:13:38,052 --> 00:13:41,052
Teachers, classmates. If I wouldn't take their crap, they made my life worse.

291
00:13:41,052 --> 00:13:47,052
So I fought with all I had. Trying to make them see me.

292
00:13:48,052 --> 00:13:50,052
And then it happened.

293
00:13:51,052 --> 00:14:05,052
Not knowing where you belong is rough on anyone.

294
00:14:06,052 --> 00:14:10,052
But it's times like that you gotta keep your eyes and ears open.

295
00:14:11,052 --> 00:14:14,052
One day, you'll find somebody who feels the same way you do.

296
00:14:15,052 --> 00:14:17,052
I'm talking to you right now, aren't I?

297
00:14:18,052 --> 00:14:20,052
That means you're not alone.

298
00:14:21,052 --> 00:14:23,052
You might forget all about me after tonight.

299
00:14:24,052 --> 00:14:29,052
But still, connecting with you over the airways is something I'll remember for life.

300
00:14:29,052 --> 00:14:35,052
And the next time you start to feel like you're alone in the world, you'll have this place to come back to.

301
00:14:36,052 --> 00:14:38,052
Ah, miss, that's mine.

302
00:14:45,052 --> 00:14:47,052
Eat this!

303
00:14:50,052 --> 00:14:54,052
One day, you'll find somebody who feels the same way you do.

304
00:14:54,052 --> 00:14:58,052
Those words are what led me to Reiko.

305
00:14:59,052 --> 00:15:03,052
Then one day, I kicked the bucket and started hanging out with dancing zombies.

306
00:15:04,052 --> 00:15:07,052
If it wasn't for Ryu, where would I be now?

307
00:15:08,052 --> 00:15:09,052
No.

308
00:15:10,052 --> 00:15:12,052
I won't let it end this way.

309
00:15:13,052 --> 00:15:18,052
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

310
00:15:18,052 --> 00:15:20,052
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

311
00:15:22,052 --> 00:15:23,052
Ah?

312
00:15:25,052 --> 00:15:26,052
Hmm?

313
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:30,052
Whoa! That is so many kinds of illegal!

314
00:15:32,052 --> 00:15:33,052
Hey, slow down!

315
00:15:34,052 --> 00:15:35,052
Nope!

316
00:15:35,052 --> 00:15:36,052
Writing double!

317
00:15:36,052 --> 00:15:37,052
Huh?

318
00:15:40,052 --> 00:15:45,052
I'm sorry, but it's an emergency.

319
00:15:45,052 --> 00:15:48,212
I'm sorry, but it's an emergency. Please don't lock us up. I'm sorry.

320
00:15:54,972 --> 00:15:57,692
And now for an encore by special request.

321
00:15:58,092 --> 00:16:00,952
I am White Ryo, and here's Do You Hate Windy Days.

322
00:16:04,072 --> 00:16:04,972
Excuse us!

323
00:16:04,972 --> 00:16:05,192
Huh?

324
00:16:05,192 --> 00:16:05,672
Huh?

325
00:16:05,672 --> 00:16:06,112
Huh?

326
00:16:06,112 --> 00:16:06,232
Huh?

327
00:16:12,232 --> 00:16:13,292
Two little kittens.

328
00:16:13,292 --> 00:16:15,672
But they don't look lost at all.

329
00:16:15,672 --> 00:16:19,492
By the way, did you hear Franshushu came back recently?

330
00:16:21,132 --> 00:16:23,752
Of course. I saw they made a post about it.

331
00:16:24,352 --> 00:16:25,992
That's really gross, you know?

332
00:16:28,332 --> 00:16:31,792
Okay. Seems like we got a warm breeze blowing today.

333
00:16:32,452 --> 00:16:33,712
Let's talk to our guests.

334
00:16:34,672 --> 00:16:36,832
We're with Franshushu. I'm number two.

335
00:16:37,672 --> 00:16:40,972
And my name is number one, sir. We're very sorry to barge in like this.

336
00:16:40,972 --> 00:16:45,012
Well, what is it then?

337
00:16:45,392 --> 00:16:47,952
I came here to say I'm not letting you quit the show.

338
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:51,092
In Saga, people feel lost and alone.

339
00:16:51,932 --> 00:16:53,912
Hell, Saga is lost and alone.

340
00:16:54,072 --> 00:16:55,752
And if you don't do your show anymore,

341
00:16:56,352 --> 00:17:00,252
if you leave, what's going to happen to Saga's burning soul?

342
00:17:00,952 --> 00:17:03,212
Listen, the only reason that I'm an idol today

343
00:17:03,212 --> 00:17:04,972
is because of things you've said.

344
00:17:04,972 --> 00:17:08,472
And there are tons of people like me all over Saga.

345
00:17:09,092 --> 00:17:11,372
No, all over Japan, even.

346
00:17:11,912 --> 00:17:14,892
That's why I beg you, do not stop the show.

347
00:17:15,692 --> 00:17:17,832
Your listeners need a place to turn to.

348
00:17:18,692 --> 00:17:19,132
Right.

349
00:17:19,552 --> 00:17:22,512
They need a home they can turn to, not this old codger.

350
00:17:22,512 --> 00:17:25,972
You thought I was just going to split?

351
00:17:26,632 --> 00:17:30,132
No, I'd rather leave this place to someone who has the passion to run it.

352
00:17:31,232 --> 00:17:34,432
I mean, hell, even my pompadour is starting to give up the ghost.

353
00:17:34,692 --> 00:17:35,512
Who are you going to...

354
00:17:36,072 --> 00:17:39,632
The answer, kiddo, is always in Saga.

355
00:17:40,392 --> 00:17:40,872
What?

356
00:17:41,712 --> 00:17:43,932
I'm thinking you gals should take over.

357
00:17:43,932 --> 00:17:49,512
Wait, you can't just...

358
00:17:49,512 --> 00:17:50,832
You're here and you're perfect.

359
00:17:51,752 --> 00:17:53,432
So why waste time deciding?

360
00:17:53,992 --> 00:17:54,612
You sure?

361
00:17:55,332 --> 00:17:58,132
You've got the kind of spark that lights a fire in others.

362
00:17:58,752 --> 00:18:00,512
You won't just lead Franshoushu.

363
00:18:01,032 --> 00:18:02,832
You'll be a leader to all of Saga.

364
00:18:06,792 --> 00:18:09,212
I'm Franshoushu's leader number two!

365
00:18:09,212 --> 00:18:12,652
I'm going to honor Ryu by taking over this radio show!

366
00:18:13,932 --> 00:18:18,372
Wow, a heads up would have been preferred, but okay.

367
00:18:18,692 --> 00:18:19,672
This is huge, man.

368
00:18:19,892 --> 00:18:21,852
And if you blink, you'll miss history.

369
00:18:24,392 --> 00:18:27,112
From now on, Saga is in your hands.

370
00:18:29,512 --> 00:18:32,192
So what are you going to do next?

371
00:18:32,872 --> 00:18:37,052
The old wind from Kyogatake is pushing me forward now

372
00:18:37,052 --> 00:18:39,832
to tell the world about this place.

373
00:18:43,932 --> 00:18:48,812
Look, Ryu, truth is, I love you, okay?

374
00:18:52,192 --> 00:18:53,352
Don't be stupid.

375
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:56,932
I'm not the person who truly needs your passion right now.

376
00:18:57,992 --> 00:19:00,572
It's all those wandering souls out there.

377
00:19:01,052 --> 00:19:03,112
No, it's Saga who needs you most.

378
00:19:03,112 --> 00:19:05,172
Right.

379
00:19:08,172 --> 00:19:10,752
Look me up after you've grown into fine women.

380
00:19:11,072 --> 00:19:13,312
You're both way too young to be my old lady.

381
00:19:13,312 --> 00:19:31,872
He was really something.

382
00:19:33,652 --> 00:19:34,612
That's for sure.

383
00:19:35,492 --> 00:19:37,692
Reiko probably found a cool guy like him.

384
00:19:37,692 --> 00:19:40,072
He said we'd see him again, right?

385
00:19:41,532 --> 00:19:43,672
Not until we grow up, technically.

386
00:19:44,652 --> 00:19:45,232
Oh, true.

387
00:19:46,312 --> 00:19:48,792
Problem is, no matter how many years pass,

388
00:19:49,352 --> 00:19:50,992
we're never going to get older.

389
00:19:51,652 --> 00:19:53,072
Because we're zombies.

390
00:19:56,472 --> 00:19:57,332
That's weird.

391
00:19:57,672 --> 00:19:58,312
I'm crying.

392
00:19:58,312 --> 00:20:03,272
Aw, Saki!

393
00:20:03,832 --> 00:20:05,152
Uh, what should I do?

394
00:20:05,432 --> 00:20:06,052
I'm sorry!

395
00:20:06,572 --> 00:20:07,232
There, there!

396
00:20:10,032 --> 00:20:11,672
I just don't get it, man.

397
00:20:11,672 --> 00:20:38,452
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

398
00:20:38,592 --> 00:20:40,112
What are you crying for, Sakura?

399
00:20:40,112 --> 00:20:41,592
I can't help it!

400
00:20:41,732 --> 00:20:44,252
I'm just sad because you're sad!

401
00:20:44,732 --> 00:20:46,132
Fine, then I'm not sad!

402
00:20:46,372 --> 00:20:47,832
Now stop crying, please!

403
00:20:52,312 --> 00:20:53,492
Aw, gross!

404
00:20:53,552 --> 00:20:54,612
You're drying up!

405
00:20:54,952 --> 00:20:56,752
Zombies aren't supposed to shed tears.

406
00:20:56,972 --> 00:20:58,652
This is how you turn into a mummy!

407
00:21:01,092 --> 00:21:03,852
We heard the radio show, and we love you ladies!

408
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:04,972
You can do it!

409
00:21:05,012 --> 00:21:06,172
We're rooting for you!

410
00:21:06,372 --> 00:21:08,432
Since I've been the leader of Franshu Shuu,

411
00:21:08,432 --> 00:21:10,972
I have let my soul burn like a flame!

412
00:21:11,752 --> 00:21:14,392
And from now on, I'm going to let it burn even brighter

413
00:21:14,392 --> 00:21:16,252
and light the way for not just my group,

414
00:21:16,332 --> 00:21:17,212
but all of Saga!

415
00:21:17,732 --> 00:21:20,332
Because then, if anybody feels lost,

416
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:22,452
my light can show them where to go!

417
00:21:22,872 --> 00:21:26,172
Just like Lakey Mari's lighthouse over at Uda no Saki!

418
00:21:27,212 --> 00:21:28,372
Here's our next song!

419
00:21:29,112 --> 00:21:30,932
It's Do You Hate Windy Days!

420
00:21:30,932 --> 00:21:48,832
Yeah!

421
00:21:48,832 --> 00:21:50,832
Oh

422
00:22:18,832 --> 00:22:22,832
That's how I can become myself

423
00:22:22,832 --> 00:22:28,832
The wind's strong, I don't like it

424
00:22:28,832 --> 00:22:32,832
It's not like this, it's not like this

425
00:22:32,832 --> 00:22:34,832
It's not like this

426
00:22:34,832 --> 00:22:40,832
Love, love, love

427
00:22:40,832 --> 00:22:44,832
I want to be with you

428
00:22:48,832 --> 00:22:52,832
So Saga can be Saga with Front Shushu

429
00:22:52,832 --> 00:22:54,832
So if you're ever feeling lost or alone

430
00:22:54,832 --> 00:22:56,832
You can come to us, we're here

431
00:23:12,832 --> 00:23:14,832
And remember, the answers you're looking for

432
00:23:14,832 --> 00:23:16,832
Can always be found here in Saga

433
00:23:18,832 --> 00:23:20,832
Yay!

434
00:23:25,832 --> 00:23:26,832
Saki here

435
00:23:26,832 --> 00:23:29,832
I swear, I'll light the way with Saga's burning soul

436
00:23:29,832 --> 00:23:30,832
We're gonna crush it

437
00:23:30,832 --> 00:23:33,832
Next time, Zombieland Saga Revenge Episode 3

438
00:23:33,832 --> 00:23:35,832
The Acoustic Saga of Love and Youth

439
00:23:35,832 --> 00:23:37,832
Be there!

